                        "form": "ро́торе"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "99ce4b0c-28c3-4eb0-b1dc-2b3b98f70dbd",
                        "entry_id": "1f842197-d80a-3825-9b66-639d6e24619f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "ро́торах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01825ad2-9012-3267-bb07-eb18f5712dda",
                        "entry_id": "1f842197-d80a-3825-9b66-639d6e24619f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "техн. вращающаяся деталь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "507c4da6-1cd1-4b87-89b6-beb9fb15bf2a",
                                "sense_id": "01825ad2-9012-3267-bb07-eb18f5712dda",
                                "text": "В порядке эксперимента городские власти решили оснастить московских дворников мотоблоками со щетками, поливалками и снегоуборочными роторами."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0a4bbd0-caed-4b98-88e8-9a62c3727236",
                                "sense_id": "01825ad2-9012-3267-bb07-eb18f5712dda",
                                "text": "Дело в том, что основной рабочий орган экскаватора ― ротор с насаженными на него ковшами, ― преодолевая огромное сопротивление грунта, может при этом смещаться по оси, что и приводит к искажениям профиля канала."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c727640-9184-3f92-845e-a5a142bf753e",
                        "entry_id": "1f842197-d80a-3825-9b66-639d6e24619f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. операция над векторным полем"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c338ec5-0a7a-40a0-9e72-ca278bc63415",
                                "sense_id": "9c727640-9184-3f92-845e-a5a142bf753e",
                                "text": "Величины потоков, циркуляции, дивергенции и ротора были рассчитаны нами численными методами."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a50eb8e9-5c37-410e-8109-009156c7773e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f842197-d80a-3825-9b66-639d6e24619f",
                        "source_sense_description": "деталь",
                        "target_lang_word": "rotor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rotor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f66210b-734a-3e4d-83c1-8a1a4a024d4c",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rotating part of a mechanical device; for example, in an electric motor, generator, alternator, or pump."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fad31ff-6f76-4080-8d99-3eab5ddfddd0",
                                                "sense_id": "5f66210b-734a-3e4d-83c1-8a1a4a024d4c",
                                                "text": "Turbines have been around for a long time—windmills and water wheels are early examples. The name comes from the Latin turbo, meaning vortex, and thus the defining property of a turbine is that a fluid or gas turns the blades of a rotor, which is attached to a shaft that can perform useful work."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49a327d3-d650-3c3d-a724-58f6ae670e4a",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rotating part of a mechanical device; for example, in an electric motor, generator, alternator, or pump.",
                                            "In a disc brake, the metal disc attached to the wheel hub."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e62c0a22-fce0-355c-9ec4-f46e52025f19",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rotating part of a mechanical device; for example, in an electric motor, generator, alternator, or pump.",
                                            "The wing of a helicopter or other rotary-wing aircraft."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe9b97cb-d515-3b05-8569-152fdf661fe9",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of powerful horizontal-axis atmospheric vortex generated by the interaction of strong winds with mountainous terrain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60f783e5-630f-4b79-a5bc-7112a2694ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "fe9b97cb-d515-3b05-8569-152fdf661fe9",
                                                "text": "A glider instructor, who had been in the COS area for more than 25 years, was interviewed. He stated that around 1200 on the day of the accident, he observed a rotor hit the ground with estimated wind speeds of 70 to 80 miles per hour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "883928da-c613-3363-9783-4db115337095",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quantity having magnitude, direction, and position."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3d2f5f8-854e-4039-9c22-a085279b9ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "883928da-c613-3363-9783-4db115337095",
                                                "text": "These quantities are unit lengths measured anywhere on the axes in the positive directions. They have magnitude, direction, and position, and are thus what I have called rotors (short for rotators) to distinguish them from vectors, which have magnitude and direction but no position."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a908993c-1852-3d78-bac4-dcd6bd636265",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of cells within an oscillator that switch between being alive and dead over the course of the oscillator's period."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f89a334d-88cf-4bae-8f65-14193d223ed0",
                                                "sense_id": "a908993c-1852-3d78-bac4-dcd6bd636265",
                                                "text": "The following figure shows examples of the most versatile class of these oscillators. The first emulates the p10 shown above; the second has period 62 and a rotor of size 10."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d8e7153-a2c6-4b9a-9e05-64b109ebb41d",
                                                "sense_id": "a908993c-1852-3d78-bac4-dcd6bd636265",
                                                "text": "The problem of determining the asymptotic colouring for a cyclic pattern from a given initial black and white pattern is completely solved. The analysis leads to the proposal of the distinction between primary and secondary rotor cells (i.e. a refinement of the classical stator-rotor distinction)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c7f8e07-0934-4f32-a702-f3e62eebe8d9",
                                                "sense_id": "a908993c-1852-3d78-bac4-dcd6bd636265",
                                                "text": "In B37/S23, it goes symmetrical after 10 ticks, and produces a familiar pair of B-heptominoes after 23 ticks (the next generation after this can be found in the rotor of a standard B3/S23 p46 oscillator):"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2194fdac-37c6-3bd7-807b-829d7a89232e",
                                        "entry_id": "164767e8-610d-36d8-a2f1-b97a4d688a4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An amusement park and carnival ride consisting of a rotating cylindrical chamber in which centrifugal force adheres riders to the wall as the floor drops away, creating a sensation of defying gravity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
